# AGENTS.md

[[.Name]] is a Weft app: Go serves the API (a `warp.App`, from `github.com/flakerimi/weft/warp`, with a list of modules) and the pages the build writes, in one binary. Weft [[.Version]] is unpacked in `.weft/`, which `weft` writes and you do not edit.
[[if .LocalGo]]Go finds Warp in `.weft/go`, which `go.mod` replaces `github.com/flakerimi/weft` with, since a development build of `weft` made this app.[[else]]Go gets Warp from GitHub: `go.mod` requires `github.com/flakerimi/weft` at the tag of this app's Weft release, and `go.sum` holds its checksums; commit both, and move the version with `weft upgrade`, not by hand.[[end]]

## Commands

```sh
weft dev        # run the app, rebuilding pages and Go as you save
weft build      # build the pages, then the binary
weft gen        # write web/.weft-types/api.ts, the typed client, from the Go
weft scaffold product name:string:required price:float   # a resource: app/products/, its test, its pages
weft routes     # every route, with its module, name and permission
weft upgrade    # move the app to the Weft version of the weft you run
weft catalog    # the components; weft catalog <Name> for one, --find <word> to search
go test ./...   # the Go tests; in a fresh clone, run weft unpack first
pnpm typecheck  # check the Vue files
```

To add a resource (a model and its five routes), run `weft scaffold` with its name and typed fields (https://weft.base.al/docs/reference/cli#weft-scaffold); it writes the pages too (a `DataTable` and the record's page), and needs `--api`, Go only, for `date` and `datetime` fields until Weft 0.2.0. To add a route, add it in a module's `Register` with `warp.Get(app, "/path", fn)`; to add a module, make `app/<name>/` with a `Module()` and list it in `app/modules.go`. `weft dev` restarts the Go server when a `.go` file or `.env` changes.

The app keeps its records in SQLite (`data.Module()`, the file `DB_URL` names in `.env`) and signs its owner in (`auth.Module()`). At its first start, while no user exists, it logs a one-time link, `/setup#token=…`, that sets the owner's password; the owner's email is `AUTH_OWNER_EMAIL` in `.env`. `GET /api/hello` answers anyone.

Until the first `weft build`, `web/dist` holds only an empty marker (`weft create` writes it, `weft unpack` puts it back in a fresh clone), so Go commands work; a binary built from it refuses to start, saying the pages are not built.

## Layout

| Path | What it is |
| --- | --- |
| `main.go`, `dist.go`, `dist_dev.go` | The server. `main.go` makes the `warp.App` and serves it; `dist.go` embeds `web/dist`; with `-tags dev`, as `weft dev` builds it, `dist_dev.go` embeds nothing |
| `app/modules.go` | The one list of the app's modules: `data`, `auth`, `hello` |
| `app/<name>/routes.go` | One module: its routes, under `/api` |
| `.env`, `.env.sample` | The settings: the port, the database, `AUTH_SECRET` and `AUTH_OWNER_EMAIL`; `.env` is not committed, `.env.sample` is and says what each one is |
| `data/` | The SQLite database, not committed |
| `web/pages/` | One page per `.vue` file; its path is the route. `login.vue` signs the owner in, `setup.vue` sets the owner's password |
| `web/components/` | Your components; an island is one used with `Island` |
| `web/session.ts` | `useSession()`: who is signed in, asked once per page; `requireUser()`; `signInAgain()` |
| `web/answers.ts` | Plain rules with no Vue: `nextPath`, `formProblem`, `sessionFrom` |
| `web/.weft-types/api.ts` | The typed client `weft gen` writes; every call to the server goes through it |

## Rules

- Call the server only through `api` from `web/.weft-types/api.ts`; never write `fetch` or a URL under `/api`.
- Use a Weft component wherever one exists: never write a raw `<button>`, `<input>`, `<select>` or `<dialog>`, and never hand-roll a menu, a popover or a date field.
- Before you write markup, run `weft catalog` for the list of components, then `weft catalog <Name>` for each one you use: its props, events, slots and an example; `weft catalog --find <word>` when you do not know the name. Never read `.weft/catalog/components.json` whole: it is too large.
- Lay pages out with `Page`, `Section`, `Stack` and `Grid`, not with custom CSS.
- Every component is `<script setup vapor lang="ts">`. Never use the Options API, `getCurrentInstance` or VNode render functions, nor another UI library.
- Weft components (`Page`, `Card`, `Button` and the rest) need no import in a `.vue` file. `useHead` is a function, so import it from `@weft/ui`.
- Styles use only `--weft-*` tokens, each with a fallback.
- Components adapt from inside; do not write a mobile variant of a component.
- Go: use the standard library and `github.com/flakerimi/weft/warp`; add a dependency only for what the standard library cannot do, such as a database driver.
- Do not edit `.weft/` or `web/.weft-types/`: `weft` writes them.

More for agents: https://weft.base.al/index.md and https://weft.base.al/llms.txt
